    "title": "Pierre Deligne Papers and Letters: Working Translation Drafts and Source/QA Packets",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21212608",
    "publication_date": "2026-07-06",
    "description": "<p>This record contains Pierre Deligne paper and letter working drafts, organized as a reader-first public surface. The latest cleanup fronts the sequential cumulative English and French readers for Papers 001-016p080, groups individual paper and letter PDFs by language, and groups TeX/source-check/QA/update material into a separate artifact ZIP.</p>\n<p><strong>Status caveat.</strong> These are useful working drafts and source/QA packets, not a critical edition and not a blanket source-faithfulness claim. Deligne material is uneven: some papers and letters are strong working drafts, while diagram-heavy and equation-dense pieces still require source comparison.</p>\n<p><strong>Use rule.</strong> Open the cumulative readers first. Use the English/French grouped PDF ZIPs for individual papers and letters. Use the TeX/source/QA ZIP for checking and repair. Check commutative diagrams, dense formulas, references, and theorem statements against source witnesses before relying on them.</p>\n<p><strong>GitHub.</strong> Corrections and pull requests can be made through <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
